+  // Camoufox: juggler's moves coalesce like real ones. A real mouse outruns the
+  // refresh driver, so the page gets one pointermove per tick carrying the
+  // rest in getCoalescedEvents(), and a pointerrawupdate per raw move; moves
+  // kept out of the queue arrived 1:1:1 instead. A juggler move is acked twice:
+  // "mousequeued" here, when the renderer has it (MouseDispatch's deadlock
+  // bound), and "mousemove" from HandleRealMouseButtonEvent when it reaches
+  // the page, which the caller's own move waits for.
